Both changes are within `crates/`, the allowed path. Only `docs/contracts/agent-loop.md` remains as an untouched pre-existing change from the prior cycle — I didn't need to modify it further since it already documents resolved-path containment generally.

Summary of the remediation for finding **F1-dangling-symlink-escape**:

1. **`crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/agent_runtime.rs`** — `canonicalize_partial` now:
   - Only walks up to a parent when the error is `ErrorKind::NotFound`; any other error (EACCES, ELOOP, etc.) propagates instead of silently falling back to a lexical re-append.
   - Before treating a not-yet-existing component as a to-be-created leaf, checks `symlink_metadata()` on it — if that succeeds, the component exists as a dangling symlink and the whole resolution is refused, rather than being re-appended literally and authorized.

2. **`crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/runtime_path_containment.rs`** — added two tests per the remediation's acceptance guidance:
   - `apply_edit_refuses_a_dangling_symlink_leaf_pointing_outside` — leaf is a dangling symlink to a non-existent outside path; asserts the write is refused and the outside target is never created.
   - `apply_edit_refuses_a_dangling_symlink_intermediate_component` — an intermediate path component is a dangling symlink; asserts the same.

All 6 active tests in the file pass (the 2 pre-existing `#[ignore]` tests belong to PRD-082 and are out of scope here), `cargo fmt --check` is clean, `cargo clippy` is clean, and the full `tests-green-crates` suite passes. No commits were made, per instructions.
